# Keep every text file on LF so diffs never fight over line endings and
# shell scripts run under Git Bash on Windows. The line-endings CI check
# catches anything that slips past this.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary

# A generated append-only list, where every release adds a line at the end
# and two of them conflict there without meaning to: a union merge keeps
# both sides' lines. It applies to merges git does locally, which includes
# the merge queue's batch branch; GitHub's own conflict check ignores it.
# Use it only for a file a tool writes. Never give it to a page agents
# edit by hand (a tasks file, a spec, the manual): the conflict is the one
# signal that two pull requests are appending to a shared page, and hiding
# it is how one project reached 64 appends to one file in a week.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
